---
import ToolingLayout from "../../layouts/ToolingLayout.astro";
---

<ToolingLayout title="User guide" currentPath="/tooling">
  <h1 class="govuk-heading-xl">User guide</h1>

  <p class="govuk-body">
    To connect to the AI Gateway you need to{" "}
    <a class="govuk-link" href="/tooling/get-your-key">
      get your AI Gateway key
    </a>
    . You can connect your key to many existing tools, for example:
  </p>

  <ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
    <li>
      <a class="govuk-link" href="/tooling/opencode">
        OpenCode
      </a>{" "}
      (a terminal-based coding agent which lets you choose different models)
    </li>
    <li>
      <a class="govuk-link" href="/tooling/claude-code">
        Claude Code
      </a>{" "}
      (a terminal-based coding agent from Anthropic)
    </li>
    <li>
      <a class="govuk-link" href="/tooling/cursor">
        Cursor
      </a>{" "}
      (a code editor built on VS Code)
    </li>
    <li>
      <a class="govuk-link" href="/tooling/pi">
        Pi
      </a>{" "}
      (a terminal-based coding agent you can customise with extensions)
    </li>
  </ul>

  <figure class="govuk-!-margin-top-6 govuk-!-margin-bottom-6">
    <img
      src="/assets/images/gateway-diagram-generic.svg"
      alt="Diagram showing your tool connecting to the AI Gateway, which then connects to multiple AI models including Claude, Gemini and others."
      class="govuk-!-width-full"
    />
  </figure>

  <p class="govuk-body">
    Your AI Gateway key gives you access to multiple models. When you submit a
    request, your tool sends it through the AI Gateway to your chosen model.
  </p>
</ToolingLayout>
